    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d842">

                <pb facs="0997" n="987" xml:id="pg987"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.6176/12–2844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-28">December 28,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10759. For Bugbee from Haley. Following advisors to Haley selected for Rubber
                    Study Group meeting: Viles,<anchor n="50" xml:id="d842-f1"/> Young,<anchor
                        n="51" xml:id="d842-f2"/> Collyer, Litchfield, Smith, Hotchkiss,<anchor
                        n="52" xml:id="d842-f3"/> Firestone,<anchor n="53" xml:id="d842-f4"/>
                        Davis,<anchor n="54" xml:id="d842-f5"/> Trimble<anchor n="55"
                        xml:id="d842-f6"/> from industry; Batt,<anchor n="56" xml:id="d842-f7"/>
                    Bicknell, Klossner<anchor n="57" xml:id="d842-f8"/> and Clark<anchor n="58"
                        xml:id="d842-f9"/> from government. Secretariat Phillips, DuBarry<anchor
                        n="59" xml:id="d842-f10"/> and Bugbee. Post conference trip to synthetic
                    plants planned for January 29 to about February 2.</p>
                <p>Department will attempt to dispatch three copies of revised report in time to
                    reach London by January 8. Revised military tire ticket requires recomputation
                    of consumption data. [Haley.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
